; The Microsoft.UI composition provider of the Microsoft.WindowsAppRuntime package.  An
; unpackaged WinUI 3 app registers its activatable classes through its framework package, so
; a prefix has no Microsoft.UI.Composition.* keys; Microsoft.ui.xaml.dll then fails the
; RoGetActivationFactory of Microsoft.UI.Composition.Compositor and FailFasts the process in
; DCompTreeHost::CreateWinRTInteropCompositionDevice.  Register the class with the builtin
; provider, in the 64-bit view combase reads, exactly as Windows does.
[DcompiActivation]
HKLM,Software\Microsoft\WindowsRuntime\ActivatableClassId\Microsoft.UI.Composition.Compositor,,16
