HKLM,Software\Microsoft\WindowsRuntime\ActivatableClassId\Microsoft.UI.Composition.Compositor,"ThreadingModel",0x10001,2

; The shell brokers a packaged (UWP) app CoCreates when it starts: the activatable application
; registrar the app hands its activation object to, the CoreWindow factory broker a view's
; CoreWindow comes from, and the process state manager's broker. Windows runs the first and the
; second out of process, in the shell; a prefix has no shell, so wineuwp.dll provides all three
; in-process. ThreadingModel Both because the activation arrives on the app's view thread.
[WineuwpActivation]
