; The app-visible probe classes of the Windows.System / Windows.Devices.Input namespaces: the
; gate traces show one 'Failed to find library' line per class (EducationSettings from client
; 042c, PenDevice from client 0468, Windows.System.User in the older-era traces), each of which
; is a RoGetActivationFactory probe that retry-loops on the REGDB_E_CLASSNOTREG answer.  Windows
; registers every activatable class under the ActivatableClassId key with its DllPath and
; ThreadingModel and combase resolves RoGetActivationFactory through it; an unpackaged prefix has
; no such registrations, so the builtin providers are seeded here in the 64-bit view combase
; reads, in the exact [ShellWinRTActivation] format.  ThreadingModel 2 (Both): the probes arrive
; on the app's UI thread and on its background/worker threads alike.
